["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/follows", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `to` Element succeeds the `from` Element, establishing a unidirectional sequence. This succession is defined as chronological, procedural, or logical. It is used to represent either a temporal order (e.g., in a workflow) or a logical order for processing and traversal (e.g., in an ordered list).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Information about the relationship between two Elements.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetType/other", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/data", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isbn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Book Number (ISBN)](https://www.isbn-international.org/content/isbn-users-manual/29) is a unique numeric identifier for monographic publications standardized by [ISO 2108](https://www.iso.org/standard/65483.html). It consists of either 10 digits (for assignments prior to January 1, 2007) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISBN is composed of five parts: a GS1 prefix, a registration group, a registrant, a publication element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9780198836063`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/plannedCurrentResponsibleAgent", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Agent", "globalId", "", ""]
